                <pb facs="0331" n="297" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg297"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adam to Mr. Sherman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Manchester,
                                Mass.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1897-07-21"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 21,
                    1897</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note to Mr. Tower,
                    No. 719, of the 2d instant, respecting the number of vessels employed on patrol
                    duties in Bering Sea during the present season, I have the honor to inform you,
                    in compliance with an instruction from the Marquis of Salisbury, that Her
                    Majesty’s Government have decided to send a third vessel, Her Majesty’s ship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Amphion</hi>, to Bering Sea, besides Her Majesty’s ships
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Wild Swan</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Pheasant.</hi></p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">C. F. Frederick
                    Adam.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
